  "verbalization": "Neridienone A is shown to have a target relationship with SNU-387, which is a compound that acts as a target of multiple molecular entities, including (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol. All these compounds share a common target, RWLeu4, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of a specific molecular pathway. The evidence indicates that Neridienone A may interact with SNU-387, which in turn targets RWLeu4, implying a possible role in the regulation of a biological process that involves the enzyme or pathway associated with RWLeu4. The consistent presence of SNU-387 as a target across multiple pathways supports the hypothesis that Neridienone A may influence the same biological process through a shared target, RWLeu4. The integration of these findings suggests a plausible mechanism of action involving the interaction between Neridienone A and SNU-387, which ultimately affects RWLeu4.",
